# Source expression language (mxeml)

Input is a **textual mathematical expression** in a **`.mxeml`** file (format `mxeml`). It must support **parentheses** and standard **operator precedence**. Evaluation is in **C**.

Nested tree text (`.teml`) and stack IR (`.eml` / `.beml`) are separate formats; see `eml-format` and `eml-cli`.

## Operators and functions

| Form | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `+` `-` `*` `/` | arithmetic |
| `^` | exponentiation |
| `log` `sin` `cos` `tan` `sqrt` `sinh` `cosh` `tanh` | functions (one parenthesized argument) |
| `eml(x, y)` | binary EML operator (exactly two comma-separated expressions) |

## Operator precedence

Parentheses change structure only (they are not syntax-tree nodes). One expression per file.

| Level | Forms | Associativity |
|---|---|---|
| Primary | number, constant, `(e)`, `func(e)`, `eml(e, e)` | n/a |
| Unary | prefix `+` `-` | right |
| Power | `^` | right |
| Mul | `*` `/` | left |
| Add | `+` `-` | left |

Examples: `1+2*3` is add(1, mul(2, 3)); `2^3^2` is pow(2, pow(3, 2)); `-2^2` is neg(pow(2, 2)). Unary functions take exactly one parenthesized argument. `eml` takes exactly two. Implicit multiplication / juxtaposition is not allowed. Top-level comma and wrong arity (`eml()`, `eml(x)`, `eml(x,y,z)`) are parse errors.

## Constants

- Decimal numbers (e.g. `3`, `3.14`)
- Exponential / scientific numbers (e.g. `1.2e-3`)
- `i` (imaginary unit)
- `pi`
- `e`
- `phi` (golden ratio)

When lowering to IR (`eml compile`), `log` is **natural log** (`ln`), matching the EML paper. Constant `phi` lowers as `(1 + sqrt(5)) / 2`. Binary `eml(x, y)` lowers to `Make_Eml(Lower(x), Lower(y), Comment => "eml")`.

`$VARNAME` is **preprocessor syntax**, not a tokenizer or parser token. Bindings
are supplied on the CLI as `--var $NAME=EXPRESSION` (or `-v`) on `preproc`,
`tokenize`, `parse`, and `compile`. EXPRESSION is pasted textually into the source before
tokenization. Unbound `$VARNAME` in the file is an error (every occurrence
reported). Unused `--var` bindings emit warnings unless `--warn none`.

Preprocessor also applies to **`.teml`** (nested tree text). On **`.eml`** / **`.beml`**, the preprocessor is off; any `--var` is unused (same warn/error modes).

After preprocessing, the mxeml language has no `$VAR` tokens.
